{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>יָדַעְתִּי כִּי טֶרֶם תִּירְאוּן</b> Ibn Ezra correctly seized upon the words of Rashi, that <b>טֶרֶם</b> is not like \"לֹא\", but rather has the sense of \"קֹדֶם\" (before). And he explained that the verse lacks one word: \"טֶרֶם זֶה תִּירְאוּן\" — that is, before I spread out my hands and the thunder and hail cease, you fear HaShem, for when the plague is removed you revert and rebel. And it is even more correct to explain that it also alludes to the earlier occasions. He says: I have already known of you that while you are not yet afraid — but afterward you rebel, for always, before the plagues depart from you, you fear HaShem as you did with the frogs (Exodus 8:4) and the mixed swarm (ibid. v. 24), and then you reverted and rebelled against the word of HaShem, and so you will always do. And because of this he did not warn him further upon his return, but rather prayed for him in the locusts, on the assumption that he would continue to sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:36.704394862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}